<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proofs</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>.
Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{2}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{2}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the outputs of layer <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">L</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for two arbitrary inputs, and define <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta z^{(i)}=z_{1}^{(i)}-z_{2}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta z^{(i)}=z_{1}^{(i)}-z_{2}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta v^{(i)}=v_{1}^{(i)}-v_{2}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta v^{(i)}=v_{1}^{(i)}-v_{2}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0\}\cup\mathbb{Z}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0\}\cup\mathbb{Z}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the stacked vector <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}=[\Delta z^{(0)^{T}},\ldots,\Delta z^{(N-1)^{T}}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}=[\Delta z^{(0)^{T}},\ldots,\Delta z^{(N-1)^{T}}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Left and right multiplying the matrix in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) by <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math> and utilizing the fact that <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta z^{(N)}=W_{N}\Delta z^{(N-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta z^{(N)}=W_{N}\Delta z^{(N-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}+\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(i-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}Y_{i}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(i-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)})&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}+\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(i-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}Y_{i}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(i-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)})&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}\triangleq\begin{bmatrix}W_{i}^{T}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}W_{i}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}W_{i}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})W_{i}&amp;\Lambda_{i}\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}\triangleq\begin{bmatrix}W_{i}^{T}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}W_{i}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}W_{i}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})W_{i}&amp;\Lambda_{i}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By the slope-restrictedness condition in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Slope-restrictedness). ‣ 2.2 Preliminaries ‣ 2 Problem Formulation and Background ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, for <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathbb{Z}_{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathbb{Z}_{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}^{i}\Delta v^{(i)}\leq\Delta z^{(i)}\leq\bm{\beta}^{i}\Delta v^{(i)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}^{i}\Delta v^{(i)}\leq\Delta z^{(i)}\leq\bm{\beta}^{i}\Delta v^{(i)}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, for any <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})&amp;\Lambda_{i}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})&amp;\Lambda_{i}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta v^{(i)}=W_{i}\Delta z^{(i-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta v^{(i)}=W_{i}\Delta z^{(i-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, this yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(i-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}Y_{i}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(i-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(i-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}Y_{i}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(i-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, every summand in (<a href="#A1.E37" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>) involving <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-positive. Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)})\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)})\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">which further gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta z^{(N)}\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{1/F}\|\Delta z^{(0)}\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta z^{(N)}\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{1/F}\|\Delta z^{(0)}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p">implying that the Lipschitz constant is at most <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{1/F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{1/F}</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span>. The proof is similar to that of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Let <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{2}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{2}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the outputs at layer <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{L}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">L</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{L}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for two arbitrary inputs, and define <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta z^{(j)}=z_{1}^{(j)}-z_{2}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta z^{(j)}=z_{1}^{(j)}-z_{2}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=p,\ldots,i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=p,\ldots,i</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the subvectors of <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta z^{(p)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta z^{(p)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta z^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta z^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> indexed by <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}\subseteq\mathbb{Z}_{d_{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}\subseteq\mathbb{Z}_{d_{p}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\subseteq\mathbb{Z}_{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\subseteq\mathbb{Z}_{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the stacked vector</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}=\left[(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})^{T},\,(\Delta z^{(p+1)})^{T},\,\ldots,\,(\Delta z^{(i-1)})^{T}\right]^{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}=\left[(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})^{T},\,(\Delta z^{(p+1)})^{T},\,\ldots,\,(\Delta z^{(i-1)})^{T}\right]^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Left and right multiplying the matrix in (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Theorem 3. ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) by <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math> yields and utilizing the fact that <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta z_{\mathcal{L}}^{(i)}=(W_{i})_{(\mathcal{L},\bullet)}\Delta z^{(i-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta z_{\mathcal{L}}^{(i)}=(W_{i})_{(\mathcal{L},\bullet)}\Delta z^{(i-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})^{T}(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})+\sum_{m=p+1}^{i-1}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(m-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}Y_{m}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(m-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}-F(\Delta z^{(i-1)}_{\mathcal{L}})^{T}((\Delta z^{(i-1)}_{\mathcal{L}})&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})^{T}(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})+\sum_{m=p+1}^{i-1}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(m-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}Y_{m}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(m-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}-F(\Delta z^{(i-1)}_{\mathcal{L}})^{T}((\Delta z^{(i-1)}_{\mathcal{L}})&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq\begin{bmatrix}W_{m}^{T}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}\Lambda_{m}D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}}W_{m}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}W_{m}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}})\Lambda_{m}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{m}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}})W_{m}&amp;\Lambda_{m}\end{bmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq\begin{bmatrix}W_{m}^{T}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}\Lambda_{m}D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}}W_{m}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}W_{m}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}})\Lambda_{m}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{m}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}})W_{m}&amp;\Lambda_{m}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p">Similarly, by the slope-restrictedness condition in Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Slope-restrictedness). ‣ 2.2 Preliminaries ‣ 2 Problem Formulation and Background ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, for each <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, and for any <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{m}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{m}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(m)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}\Lambda_{m}D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}})\Lambda_{m}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{m}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}})&amp;\Lambda_{m}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(m)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(m)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}\Lambda_{m}D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}})\Lambda_{m}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{m}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{m}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{m}})&amp;\Lambda_{m}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(m)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.5" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta v^{(m)}=W_{m}\Delta z^{(m-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta v^{(m)}=W_{m}\Delta z^{(m-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, this yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(m-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}Y_{m}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(m-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(m-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}Y_{m}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta z^{(m-1)}\\
\Delta z^{(m)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.6" class="ltx_p">Therefore, all terms involving <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A1.E38" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) are non-positive.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})^{T}(\Lambda_{p})_{(\mathcal{K},\mathcal{K})}(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})-F(\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}})^{T}\left(W_{i}\right)_{(\mathcal{L},\bullet)}^{T}\left(W_{i}\right)_{(\mathcal{L},\bullet)}(\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}})\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})^{T}(\Lambda_{p})_{(\mathcal{K},\mathcal{K})}(\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}})-F(\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}})^{T}\left(W_{i}\right)_{(\mathcal{L},\bullet)}^{T}\left(W_{i}\right)_{(\mathcal{L},\bullet)}(\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}})\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}})=\left(W_{i}\right)_{(\mathcal{L},\bullet)}\Delta z^{(i-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}})=\left(W_{i}\right)_{(\mathcal{L},\bullet)}\Delta z^{(i-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>, this further gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}}\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{1/F}\|\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}}\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta z^{(i)}_{\mathcal{L}}\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{1/F}\|\Delta z^{(p)}_{\mathcal{K}}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">establishing that inequality (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) holds. ∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span>.
The result follows by applying Lemma 2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Agarwal et al. (2019)</a></cite> to the symmetric block tridiagonal matrix in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). By Lemma 2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Agarwal et al. (2019)</a></cite>, a symmetric block tri-diagonal matrix defined as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{1}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{2}&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;&amp;0\\
\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{2}^{T}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{2}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{3}&amp;\cdots&amp;&amp;0\\
0&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{3}^{T}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{3}&amp;\cdots&amp;&amp;0\\
&amp;&amp;\vdots&amp;&amp;&amp;\\
0&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{N-1}^{T}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{N-1}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{N}\\
0&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{N}^{T}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{N}\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>3</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>⋯</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mtd><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{1}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{2}&amp;0&amp;\cdots&amp;&amp;0\\
\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{2}^{T}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{2}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{3}&amp;\cdots&amp;&amp;0\\
0&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{3}^{T}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{3}&amp;\cdots&amp;&amp;0\\
&amp;&amp;\vdots&amp;&amp;&amp;\\
0&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{N-1}^{T}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{N-1}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{N}\\
0&amp;\cdots&amp;0&amp;0&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{N}^{T}&amp;\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{N}\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">is positive definite if and only if</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{X}_{i}&gt;0,\quad\forall i\in\{0\}\cup\mathbb{Z}_{l-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{X}_{i}&gt;0,\quad\forall i\in\{0\}\cup\mathbb{Z}_{l-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{X}_{i}=\begin{cases}\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{i}&amp;\text{if }i=0,\\
\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{i}-\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{i}^{T}\widetilde{X}_{i-1}^{-1}\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{i}&amp;\text{if}\ i\in\mathbb{Z}_{l-1}.\\
\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{X}_{i}=\begin{cases}\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{i}&amp;\text{if }i=0,\\
\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{i}-\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{i}^{T}\widetilde{X}_{i-1}^{-1}\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{i}&amp;\text{if}\ i\in\mathbb{Z}_{l-1}.\\
\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.4" class="ltx_p">For our matrix, we directly substitute <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{i},\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathcal{P}}_{i},\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{i},\mathcal{R}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{i},\mathcal{R}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) and we have the result that
the block tridiagonal matrix in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) is positive definite if and only if the sequence of inequalities in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) holds, with <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In Theorem 4. ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>). ∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>.
Applying the Schur complement to the LMI in (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) with slope bounds <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>adj</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\beta}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>adj</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\beta}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}</annotation></semantics></math> directly gives an equivalent condition to be
<math id="A1.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}-c_{i}W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}-c_{i}W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i}\;=\;\Lambda_{i}-\frac{1}{4}\,\Lambda_{i}\,(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}})\,W_{i}\,(X_{i-1})^{-1}\,W_{i}^{T}\,(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}})\,\Lambda_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>adj</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>adj</mi></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>adj</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>adj</mi></mrow></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i}\;=\;\Lambda_{i}-\frac{1}{4}\,\Lambda_{i}\,(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}})\,W_{i}\,(X_{i-1})^{-1}\,W_{i}^{T}\,(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i,\mathrm{adj}}})\,\Lambda_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">This holds if and only if
<math id="A1.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{\sigma_{\max}\!\left(W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1}\,M_{i}^{-1}\,\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{\sigma_{\max}\!\left(W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1}\,M_{i}^{-1}\,\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math>
According to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Lemma 1 in ( ) ). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}\!\left(W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1}\,M_{i}^{-1}\,\right)=\sigma_{\max}\!\left(W_{i+1}\,M_{i}^{-1}\,W_{i+1}^{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}\!\left(W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1}\,M_{i}^{-1}\,\right)=\sigma_{\max}\!\left(W_{i+1}\,M_{i}^{-1}\,W_{i+1}^{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>.
By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>,
with <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathbb{Z}_{N-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathbb{Z}_{N-2}</annotation></semantics></math>, it remains to prove that <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{N-1}-FW_{N}^{T}W_{N}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{N-1}-FW_{N}^{T}W_{N}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. This is equivalent to
<math id="A1.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{l-1}/F&gt;W_{N}^{T}W_{N}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{l-1}/F&gt;W_{N}^{T}W_{N}.</annotation></semantics></math> Then, the smallest possible <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/F</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{max}(W_{N}^{T}W_{N}(M_{N-1})^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{max}(W_{N}^{T}W_{N}(M_{N-1})^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (LipSDP). ‣ 2.2 Preliminaries ‣ 2 Problem Formulation and Background ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the tightest upper bound for the Lipschitz constant is then <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{1/F}=\sqrt{\sigma_{max}(W_{N}^{T}W_{N}(M_{N-1})^{-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{1/F}=\sqrt{\sigma_{max}(W_{N}^{T}W_{N}(M_{N-1})^{-1})}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Lemma 1 in ( ) ). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and the fact that <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{N-1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{N-1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> , we have the certified Lipschitz constant to be <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\sigma_{max}(W_{N}(M_{N-1})^{-1})W_{N}^{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\sigma_{max}(W_{N}(M_{N-1})^{-1})W_{N}^{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5 (Monotonicity of Estimates with Respect to Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.2 Utilizing Local Information ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></span>.
Let <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\bm{\alpha}}^{i},\hat{\bm{\beta}}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\bm{\alpha}}^{i},\hat{\bm{\beta}}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tilde{\bm{\alpha}}^{i},\tilde{\bm{\beta}}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tilde{\bm{\alpha}}^{i},\tilde{\bm{\beta}}^{i}\}_{i=1}^{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math> be two sets of slope bounds for the activation functions, where for some <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j,i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j,i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\subset[\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\subset[\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>, and all other entries are identical. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{F}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the maximal values such that the matrix inequalities in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) are satisfied for the respective choices of slope bounds. Adopting the notations in the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we left and right multiply the matrix in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 2 (Hetereogeneous Slope Bounds). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) by <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mathbf{z}=[\Delta z^{(0)^{T}},\ldots,\Delta z^{(N-1)^{T}}]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mathbf{z}=[\Delta z^{(0)^{T}},\ldots,\Delta z^{(N-1)^{T}}]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and obtain</p>
<table id="A1.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}+\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})&amp;\Lambda_{i}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)})&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝜶</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝜷</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝜶</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msup></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝜷</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝜶</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msup></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝜷</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">v</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}+\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})&amp;\Lambda_{i}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)})&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">For the second term in (<a href="#A1.E39" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>), for each layer <math id="A1.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">L</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})&amp;\Lambda_{i}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})&amp;\Lambda_{i}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v^{(i)}\\
\Delta z^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p12.2" class="ltx_p">Expanding this block-diagonal form, with <math id="A1.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{j}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{j}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> being the <math id="A1.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{th}</annotation></semantics></math> diagonal entry of <math id="A1.SS1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain equivalently</p>
<table id="A1.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{j}^{(i)}(\alpha_{j}^{i},\beta_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})\triangleq\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v_{j}^{(i)}\\
\Delta z_{j}^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}\alpha_{j}^{i}\lambda_{j}^{i}\beta_{j}^{i}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(\alpha_{j}^{i}+\beta_{j}^{i})\lambda_{j}^{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}(\alpha_{j}^{i}+\beta_{j}^{i})\lambda_{j}^{i}&amp;\lambda_{j}^{i}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v_{j}^{(i)}\\
\Delta z_{j}^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≜</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{j}^{(i)}(\alpha_{j}^{i},\beta_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})\triangleq\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v_{j}^{(i)}\\
\Delta z_{j}^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}^{T}\begin{bmatrix}\alpha_{j}^{i}\lambda_{j}^{i}\beta_{j}^{i}&amp;-\frac{1}{2}(\alpha_{j}^{i}+\beta_{j}^{i})\lambda_{j}^{i}\\
-\frac{1}{2}(\alpha_{j}^{i}+\beta_{j}^{i})\lambda_{j}^{i}&amp;\lambda_{j}^{i}\end{bmatrix}\begin{bmatrix}\Delta v_{j}^{(i)}\\
\Delta z_{j}^{(i)}\end{bmatrix}\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p12.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{i,1}=\{j:[\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\subset[\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{i,1}=\{j:[\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\subset[\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{i,2}=\{j:[\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i}]=[\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{i,2}=\{j:[\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i}]=[\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we split (<a href="#A1.E40" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>) as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\alpha_{j}^{i},\beta_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{J}_{i,1}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\alpha_{j}^{i},\beta_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{J}_{i,2}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\alpha_{j}^{i},\beta_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})\leq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\alpha_{j}^{i},\beta_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})=\sum_{j\in\mathcal{J}_{i,1}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\alpha_{j}^{i},\beta_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{J}_{i,2}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\alpha_{j}^{i},\beta_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{J}_{i,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{J}_{i,1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\subset[\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i}]\subset[\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>. With the slope bounds assumption as in Assumption (<a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Slope-restrictedness). ‣ 2.2 Preliminaries ‣ 2 Problem Formulation and Background ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and <math id="A1.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{j}^{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{j}^{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq Q_{j}^{(i)}(\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})\leq Q_{j}^{(i)}(\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i}),\quad\forall\Delta v_{j}^{(i)},\Delta z_{j}^{(i)},\lambda_{j}^{i}\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq Q_{j}^{(i)}(\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})\leq Q_{j}^{(i)}(\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i}),\quad\forall\Delta v_{j}^{(i)},\Delta z_{j}^{(i)},\lambda_{j}^{i}\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p13.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A1.SS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{J}_{i,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{J}_{i,2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{j}^{(i)}(\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})=Q_{j}^{(i)}(\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{j}^{(i)}(\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})=Q_{j}^{(i)}(\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Then, for all <math id="A1.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta v^{(i)},\Delta z^{(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta v^{(i)},\Delta z^{(i)})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})\leq\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})\leq\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p14.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting the above inequality into (<a href="#A1.E39" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>), we have, for any fixed choice of <math id="A1.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Lambda_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Lambda_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\tilde{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\tilde{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}+\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\Delta z^{(0)})^{T}\Delta z^{(0)}+\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\sum_{j=1}^{d_{i}}Q_{j}^{(i)}(\hat{\alpha}_{j}^{i},\hat{\beta}_{j}^{i},\lambda_{j}^{i})-F(\Delta z^{(N)})^{T}(\Delta z^{(N)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">This means that for any fixed choice of <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Lambda_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Lambda_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, the largest value <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and the largest value <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}</annotation></semantics></math> such that (<a href="#A1.E39" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) holds with slope bounds <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tilde{\bm{\alpha}}^{i},\tilde{\bm{\beta}}^{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tilde{\bm{\alpha}}^{i},\tilde{\bm{\beta}}^{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{\bm{\alpha}}^{i},\hat{\bm{\beta}}^{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{\bm{\alpha}}^{i},\hat{\bm{\beta}}^{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, satisfy</p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{F}(\{\Lambda_{i}\})\geq\hat{F}(\{\Lambda_{i}\})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{F}(\{\Lambda_{i}\})\geq\hat{F}(\{\Lambda_{i}\}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p15.2" class="ltx_p">Consequently, taking the supremum over all choices <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Lambda_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Lambda_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{F}^{*}\geq\hat{F}^{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{F}^{*}\geq\hat{F}^{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p15.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{F}^{*}=\sup_{\{\Lambda_{i}\}}\tilde{F}(\{\Lambda_{i}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{F}^{*}=\sup_{\{\Lambda_{i}\}}\tilde{F}(\{\Lambda_{i}\})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{F}^{*}=\sup_{\{\Lambda_{i}\}}F(\{\Lambda_{i}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{F}^{*}=\sup_{\{\Lambda_{i}\}}F(\{\Lambda_{i}\})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the corresponding Lipschitz upper bounds satisfy
<math id="A1.SS1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{1/\tilde{F}^{*}}\leq\sqrt{1/\hat{F}^{*}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{1/\tilde{F}^{*}}\leq\sqrt{1/\hat{F}^{*}}.</annotation></semantics></math> ∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6 (First-order Method via Mean Value Theorem). ‣ 3.2 Utilizing Local Information ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></span>.
Let <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathcal{Z}=\mathcal{B}(z_{c},\delta_{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathcal{Z}=\mathcal{B}(z_{c},\delta_{z})</annotation></semantics></math>, and define <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta z=z-z_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta z=z-z_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Clarke’s Mean Value Theorem, for any <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z,z_{c}\in\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z,z_{c}\in\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=z_{c}+t(z-z_{c})\in\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=z_{c}+t(z-z_{c})\in\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\partial g(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\partial g(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(z)-g(z_{c})=v^{T}(z-z_{c})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(z)-g(z_{c})=v^{T}(z-z_{c}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p17.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial g(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial g(X)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Clarke subdifferential of <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A1.SS1.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial g(X):=\texttt{co}\left\{\lim_{k\to\infty}\nabla g(z_{k}):z_{k}\to X,\;g\text{ differentiable at }z_{k}\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">co</mtext><mrow><mo>{</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>g</mi><mtext> differentiable at </mtext><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial g(X):=\texttt{co}\left\{\lim_{k\to\infty}\nabla g(z_{k}):z_{k}\to X,\;g\text{ differentiable at }z_{k}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p17.3" class="ltx_p">with <span id="A1.SS1.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">co</span> denoting the convex hull.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Lipschitz with constant <span id="A1.SS1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">L</span> over <math id="A1.SS1.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="A1.SS1.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\partial g(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\partial g(X)</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A1.SS1.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathcal{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathcal{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g(z)-g(z_{c})|\leq\textbf{L}\|\delta z\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">L</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g(z)-g(z_{c})|\leq\textbf{L}\|\delta z\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p18.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(z_{c})-\textbf{L}\|\delta z\|_{2}\leq g(z)\leq g(z_{c})+\textbf{L}\|\delta z\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">L</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">L</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(z_{c})-\textbf{L}\|\delta z\|_{2}\leq g(z)\leq g(z_{c})+\textbf{L}\|\delta z\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p18.3" class="ltx_p">which is exactly (<a href="#S3.E20" title="In Theorem 6 (First-order Method via Mean Value Theorem). ‣ 3.2 Utilizing Local Information ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ 3.2 Utilizing Local Information ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></span>.
We require <math id="A1.SS1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\alpha^{i}_{l},\beta^{i}_{l}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\alpha^{i}_{l},\beta^{i}_{l}]</annotation></semantics></math> to contain all subgradients of <math id="A1.SS1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A1.SS1.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math>, that is,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{v\in[a,b]}\partial\phi(v)\subseteq[\alpha^{i}_{l},\beta^{i}_{l}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{v\in[a,b]}\partial\phi(v)\subseteq[\alpha^{i}_{l},\beta^{i}_{l}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p19.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the minimal (tightest) interval is naturally given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{i}_{l}=\inf_{v\in[a,b]}\inf\{\partial\phi(v)\},\quad\beta^{i}_{l}=\sup_{v\in[a,b]}\sup\{\partial\phi(v)\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{i}_{l}=\inf_{v\in[a,b]}\inf\{\partial\phi(v)\},\quad\beta^{i}_{l}=\sup_{v\in[a,b]}\sup\{\partial\phi(v)\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p19.3" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4. ‣ 3.3 ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Scalable and Accurate Algorithm for Local Lipschitz Estimates ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span>.
Observe that for any row index <math id="A1.SS1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A1.SS1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th diagonal entry of <math id="A1.SS1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}(M_{i-1})^{-1}W_{i}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(M_{i-1})^{-1}W_{i}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(W_{i}(M_{i-1})^{-1}W_{i}^{T}\right)_{(l,l)}=(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(W_{i}(M_{i-1})^{-1}W_{i}^{T}\right)_{(l,l)}=(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p20.2" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Lemma 1 in ( ) ). ‣ 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, if <math id="A1.SS1.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{i-1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{i-1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS1.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AA^{T}(M_{i-1})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AA^{T}(M_{i-1})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(M_{i-1})^{-1}A^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(M_{i-1})^{-1}A^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> share the same nonzero eigenvalues for any matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this to the row vector <math id="A1.SS1.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that
<math id="A1.SS1.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="A1.SS1.p20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>
share the same nonzero eigenvalues.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\max}\left((W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}\right)=\sigma_{\max}\left((W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}\right)=(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\max}\left((W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}\right)=\sigma_{\max}\left((W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}\right)=(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p21.2" class="ltx_p">The last equality holds as <math id="A1.SS1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a scalar.
Combining with (<a href="#A1.E41" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) completes the proof. ∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 3.3 ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Scalable and Accurate Algorithm for Local Lipschitz Estimates ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>.
Notice that for each <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,\ldots,d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,\ldots,d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{d}^{(i)}_{l}=\left(W_{i}(M_{i-1})^{-1}W_{i}^{T}\right)_{(l,l)}=(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{d}^{(i)}_{l}=\left(W_{i}(M_{i-1})^{-1}W_{i}^{T}\right)_{(l,l)}=(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}(M_{i-1})^{-1}(W_{i})_{(l,\bullet)}^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p22.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}=(M_{i-1})^{-1}W_{i}^{T}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{i-1}\times d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=(M_{i-1})^{-1}W_{i}^{T}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{i-1}\times d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for each <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{d}^{(i)}_{l}=\sum_{k=1}^{d_{i-1}}(W_{i})_{(l,k)}(A_{i})_{(k,l)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐝</mi><mi>l</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munderover><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{d}^{(i)}_{l}=\sum_{k=1}^{d_{i-1}}(W_{i})_{(l,k)}(A_{i})_{(k,l)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p22.3" class="ltx_p">Now, observe that <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{i})_{(\bullet,k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{i})_{(\bullet,k)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th column of <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{i})_{(k,\bullet)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{i})_{(k,\bullet)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The elementwise product <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{i})_{(\bullet,k)}\otimes\left((A_{i})_{(k,\bullet)}\right)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{i})_{(\bullet,k)}\otimes\left((A_{i})_{(k,\bullet)}\right)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a vector in <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th entry is <math id="A1.SS1.p22.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{i})_{(l,k)}(A_{i})_{(k,l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{i})_{(l,k)}(A_{i})_{(k,l)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p23.1" class="ltx_p">Summing over <math id="A1.SS1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A1.SS1.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{d}^{(i)}=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{d_{i-1}}(W_{i})_{(\bullet,k)}\otimes\left((A_{i})_{(k,\bullet)}\right)^{T}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐝</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∙</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{d}^{(i)}=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{d_{i-1}}(W_{i})_{(\bullet,k)}\otimes\left((A_{i})_{(k,\bullet)}\right)^{T},</annotation></semantics></math>
which establishes (<a href="#S3.E24" title="In Lemma 2. ‣ 3.3 ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Scalable and Accurate Algorithm for Local Lipschitz Estimates ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>).
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition5" title="Proposition 5. ‣ 3.4.1 Acceleration in Special Cases ‣ 3.4 Acceleration and Stability Safeguards ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</span>
For each <math id="A1.SS1.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{i,\ldots,i+p\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{i,\ldots,i+p\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}^{j}=\bm{\beta}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}^{j}=\bm{\beta}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, layer <math id="A1.SS1.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{L}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">L</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{L}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> acts as</p>
<table id="A1.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(j)}=D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}v^{(j)}=D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\left(W_{j}z^{(j-1)}+b_{j}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(j)}=D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}v^{(j)}=D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\left(W_{j}z^{(j-1)}+b_{j}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p24.2" class="ltx_p">We prove (<a href="#S3.E29" title="In Proposition 5. ‣ 3.4.1 Acceleration in Special Cases ‣ 3.4 Acceleration and Stability Safeguards ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) by induction on <math id="A1.SS1.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\{1,\ldots,p\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\{1,\ldots,p\}</annotation></semantics></math> that</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{(i+s)}=\tilde{W}_{i+s}\,z^{(i-1)}+\tilde{b}_{i+s}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{(i+s)}=\tilde{W}_{i+s}\,z^{(i-1)}+\tilde{b}_{i+s},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p25.1" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{i+s}=\left(\prod_{j=i}^{i+s-1}W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\right)W_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{i+s}=\left(\prod_{j=i}^{i+s-1}W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\right)W_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{b}_{i+s}=\sum_{k=1}^{s+1}\left[\prod_{j=i+k-1}^{i+s-1}\left(W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\right)b_{i+k-1}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{b}_{i+s}=\sum_{k=1}^{s+1}\left[\prod_{j=i+k-1}^{i+s-1}\left(W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\right)b_{i+k-1}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p25.2" class="ltx_p">where the product <math id="A1.SS1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to the identity matrix if <math id="A1.SS1.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=s+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=s+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p26.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.SS1.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1</annotation></semantics></math>, at layer <math id="A1.SS1.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{L}_{j+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">L</mtext><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{L}_{j+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{(j+1)}=W_{j+1}z^{(j)}+b_{j+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{(j+1)}=W_{j+1}z^{(j)}+b_{j+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p26.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting (<a href="#A1.E42" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) into <math id="A1.SS1.p26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{(j+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{(j+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> directly gives</p>
<table id="A1.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{(j+1)}=W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\left(W_{j}z^{(j-1)}+b_{j}\right)+b_{j+1}=\underbrace{W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}W_{j}}_{\triangleq\,\tilde{W}_{j+1}}z^{(j-1)}+\underbrace{W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}b_{j}+b_{j+1}}_{\triangleq\,\tilde{b}_{j+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.448em">≜</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.448em">≜</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{(j+1)}=W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\left(W_{j}z^{(j-1)}+b_{j}\right)+b_{j+1}=\underbrace{W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}W_{j}}_{\triangleq\,\tilde{W}_{j+1}}z^{(j-1)}+\underbrace{W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}b_{j}+b_{j+1}}_{\triangleq\,\tilde{b}_{j+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p27" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p27.1" class="ltx_p">Now assume (<a href="#A1.E43" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>)-(<a href="#A1.E45" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) holds for <math id="A1.SS1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <math id="A1.SS1.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}=\bm{\beta}^{i+s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}=\bm{\beta}^{i+s}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E48X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v^{(i+s+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v^{(i+s+1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{i+s+1}z^{(i+s)}+b_{i+s+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{i+s+1}z^{(i+s)}+b_{i+s+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E48Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}v^{(i+s)}+b_{i+s+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}v^{(i+s)}+b_{i+s+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E48Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}\tilde{W}_{i+s}\,z^{(i-1)}+W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}\tilde{b}_{i+s}+b_{i+s+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}\tilde{W}_{i+s}\,z^{(i-1)}+W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}\tilde{b}_{i+s}+b_{i+s+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p27.2" class="ltx_p">By induction, we have</p>
<table id="A1.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{i+s+1}=W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}\tilde{W}_{i+s}=\left(\prod_{j=i}^{i+s}W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\right)W_{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{i+s+1}=W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}\tilde{W}_{i+s}=\left(\prod_{j=i}^{i+s}W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\right)W_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p27.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A1.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{b}_{i+s+1}=W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}\tilde{b}_{i+s}+b_{i+s+1}=\sum_{k=1}^{s+1}\left[\prod_{j=i+k-1}^{i+s-1}\left(W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\right)b_{i+k-1}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{b}_{i+s+1}=W_{i+s+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i+s}}\tilde{b}_{i+s}+b_{i+s+1}=\sum_{k=1}^{s+1}\left[\prod_{j=i+k-1}^{i+s-1}\left(W_{j+1}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{j}}\right)b_{i+k-1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p27.4" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition6" title="Proposition 6 (Unboundedness of Λ_𝑖 on Equal Slope Bounds Subset). ‣ 3.4.2 Numerical Instability in Degenerate Slope Bounds ‣ 3.4 Acceleration and Stability Safeguards ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</span>
We first show that the feasible set is non-empty and the maximum of <math id="A1.SS1.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be attained. As the feasible set with strict inequalities is open, we consider the closed relaxation of (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{c_{i},\Lambda_{i}}\;\;c_{i}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\begin{bmatrix}\Lambda_{i}-c_{i}W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1}&amp;\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})W_{i}\\
\frac{1}{2}W_{i}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}&amp;X_{i-1}\end{bmatrix}\geq 0,\;\;\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+},\;\;c_{i}\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.727em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{c_{i},\Lambda_{i}}\;\;c_{i}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\begin{bmatrix}\Lambda_{i}-c_{i}W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1}&amp;\frac{1}{2}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})W_{i}\\
\frac{1}{2}W_{i}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}&amp;X_{i-1}\end{bmatrix}\geq 0,\;\;\Lambda_{i}\in\mathbb{D}_{+},\;\;c_{i}\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p28.2" class="ltx_p">Select an <math id="A1.SS1.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS1.p28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\min\!\{1,\,2/\sigma_{max}((D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})W_{i}X_{i-1}^{-1}W_{i}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}))\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;\min\!\{1,\,2/\sigma_{max}((D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})W_{i}X_{i-1}^{-1}W_{i}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}))\}</annotation></semantics></math> and let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{i}=\varepsilon I,\qquad c_{i}=\frac{\varepsilon}{4\,\sigma_{max}(W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{i}=\varepsilon I,\qquad c_{i}=\frac{\varepsilon}{4\,\sigma_{max}(W_{i+1}^{T}W_{i+1})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p28.3" class="ltx_p">Applying the Schur complement to the LMI in (<a href="#A1.E51" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) with the fact that <math id="A1.SS1.p28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i-1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i-1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that (<a href="#A1.E51" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) is strictly feasible. Thus Slater’s condition holds, implying that the feasible set of (<a href="#A1.E51" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) is closed and convex. As the objective is linear, and the optimal value is finite, we conclude that the maximum <math id="A1.SS1.p28.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is attainable.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p29" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p29.2" class="ltx_p">Denote <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(c_{i}^{*},\Lambda_{i}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{i}^{*},\Lambda_{i}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> to be an optimal solution. Now we prove that for any <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{i}&gt;\Lambda_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{i}&gt;\Lambda_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, the constraints in (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) are all satisfied. Note that constraints on <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are automatically satisfied and we focus on the LMI. The LMI in (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In 3.1 SDP-based Lipschitz Estimates with General Slope Bounds and Arbitrary Input-Output Indices ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) is equivalent to the following statement. For any <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\begin{bmatrix}x\\
y\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{i}+d_{i-1}}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\begin{bmatrix}x\\
y\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{i}+d_{i-1}}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.E52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E52X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x^{T}\Lambda_{i}x-c_{i}\,(W_{i+1}x)^{T}(W_{i+1}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x^{T}\Lambda_{i}x-c_{i}\,(W_{i+1}x)^{T}(W_{i+1}x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}x^{T}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})W_{i}y+\frac{1}{2}y^{T}W_{i}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}x^{T}\Lambda_{i}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})W_{i}y+\frac{1}{2}y^{T}W_{i}^{T}(D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}+D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}})\Lambda_{i}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E52Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+y^{T}\!\Big(M_{i-1}+W_{i}^{T}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}W_{i}\Big)y\;&gt;\;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+y^{T}\!\Big(M_{i-1}+W_{i}^{T}D_{\bm{\alpha}^{i}}\Lambda_{i}D_{\bm{\beta}^{i}}W_{i}\Big)y\;&gt;\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p29.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{i}\subsetneqq\mathbb{Z}_{d_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⫋</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{i}\subsetneqq\mathbb{Z}_{d_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the index set where <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\alpha}^{i})_{\mathcal{J}_{i}}=(\bm{\beta}^{i})_{\mathcal{J}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\alpha}^{i})_{\mathcal{J}_{i}}=(\bm{\beta}^{i})_{\mathcal{J}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{i}\triangleq\mathbb{Z}_{d_{i}}\backslash\mathcal{J}_{i}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{i}\triangleq\mathbb{Z}_{d_{i}}\backslash\mathcal{J}_{i}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.
We further split the left hand side of (<a href="#A1.E52" title="In A.1 Proofs ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) by index sets <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p29.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex42X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
