<div id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p33" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2 of Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Scalability, Efficiency, and Tightness on Randomly Generated Networks ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ ECLipsE-Gen-Local: Efficient Compositional Local Lipschitz Estimates for Deep Neural Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>:</span> We now present the complete results for large networks, where the number of layers is chosen from <math id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{30,40,50,60,70\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>70</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{30,40,50,60,70\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and number of neurons is chosen from <math id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{60,80,100,120\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>120</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{60,80,100,120\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
